{
  "title": "Leiomyosarcoma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8058/leiomyosarcoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Leiomyosarcoma is an aggressive sarcoma thought to arise from the smooth muscle cells lining small blood vessels.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in patients in the 5th and 6th decades of life, with pain and a palpable mass.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with biopsy showing a spindle cell neoplasm with similar characteristics shared between the osseous and soft tissue forms of this disease. Immunostains are positive for actin and vimentin.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally wide surgical resection with radiation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fewer than 100 case reports of extra-facial leiomyosarcoma of bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the mean age of presentation is in 5th and 6th decades of life",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most frequently occurs in the **metaphysis of long bones**, but can occur in diaphyseal locations.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "the most frequent sites of boney presentation are the femur, tibia, ilium, and humerus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bone pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "palpable mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typical duration of symptoms prior to diagnosis is 6 months",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pelvic masses can be difficult to appreciate on inspection exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can be tender or nontender to palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "masses will be firm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "involved extremity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8058/images/humerus%20xray.jpg",
                  "caption": "AP xray of the right humerus showing a lytic, permeative lesion of the right proximal humerus."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**purely osteolytic lesions with** ill-distinct margins, moth-eaten, or permeative pattern of bone destruction.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "primarily intra-medullary but may extend into the soft tissues.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "chest",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indicated for all staging of tumors to evaluate for lung metastasis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "help evaluate bone loss of involved extremity or pelvis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "chest CT indicated in all patients as part of staging workup to evaluate for metastasis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "differentiate from benign soft tissue tumors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "evaluate size, depth, and surrounding anatomy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**appears dark on T1, similar to muscle tissue**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8058/images/mri%20t1%20lms.jpg",
                      "caption": "This coronal T1 knee image shows a low signal mass in the fibular head."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "appears heterogeneous on T2 with areas of increased signal intensity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8058/images/t2%20mri%20lms.jpg",
                      "caption": "Sagittal section of a T2 sequence for a knee showing a large mass in the fibular head."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "contrast causes diffuse enhancement of signal within the lesion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a **spindle cell neoplasm** with similar characteristics shared between the osseous and soft tissue forms of this disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8058/images/histolgy%201.jpg",
                  "caption": "Histology of a leimyosarcoma showing pink staining cells arranged into fascicles."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cigar-shaped nuclei",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**cells arranged into fascicles** along with myofibrils running parallel",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**presence of actin and vimentin immunoreactivity**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8058/images/histo%204.jpg",
                  "caption": "Vimentin staining leiomyosarcoma."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Staging",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "all tumors should be staged appropriately prior to treatment initiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "chemotherapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "diffuse metastatic disease to the lungs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "large pelvic masses with neurovascular involvement that preclude safe resection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "variable response to chemotherapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "better survival when chemotherapy combined with surgery than surgery alone",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "radiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "controversial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "contaminated resection bed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "variable response, difficult to predict",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "early wide resection of the primary lesion and secondary reconstruction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "standard of care in localized disease",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "clean margin is an important goal of surgical resection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "chemotherapy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Neo-adjuvant or adjuvant chemo/radiotherapy in the treatment of leiomyosarcoma of bone is controversial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "radiation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if unable to obtain wide margin consider adjuvant radiation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "LMS of bone in adults",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "25% recurrence rate and 25% metastasis rate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "75% survival at 3 years with treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
